From 6734e0b912a8961bc8cfe8370c1ccacbaa3631c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:05:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] DJ booth: a playable turntable with scratching, pitch,
 hot cues and FX
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Booth (dashboard, hanns_screen_program.js)
- grab the record and scratch: platter speed is sampled every 30 ms and
  streamed to the projector; on release the needle drops where you let go
- START/STOP, 33/45, pitch fader ±8/±16 % with reset, 5 s nudge,
  strobe ring, tone arm, LCD time readout
- 4 hot cues (tap set / tap jump / hold clear), FX pads: air horn,
  siren, rewind (back to cue A), brake (fade + stop)
- 'Hear FX here' monitors effects locally; keys: Space, 1-4, Q W E R, arrows

Sound (new hanns_dj_fx.js): Web Audio scratch voice + pads, no samples

Server (screenart)
- media: rate (0.5-2.0, rate-aware position), seek_rev, cue_set/cue_clear
- POST s/<token>/dj/fx/: validated effect fanned out over the screen
  socket, never stored
Projector: setPlaybackRate, jumps on seek_rev, ducks the track while
scratching, fades on brake, plays the effects; hanns_screen.js forwards dj_fx
